# Netlify-format headers. Vercel ignores this file; the headers that actually
# ship come from vercel.json.
#
# Content-Security-Policy is NOT set here. It is generated into index.html at
# build time from VITE_API_URL (see vite.config.ts), so `connect-src` always
# matches the API origin the bundle actually calls. Hardcoding it in a static
# header file is what blocked production: `connect-src 'self'
# http://localhost:4000` refused the deployed API.
/* 
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), browsing-topics=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
